From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 21:40:37 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 016/220] [ae-patch] Add a Paste button to the web terminal on
 touch devices

On an iPhone a long press on the web terminal offers no Paste: xterm.js
draws on a canvas and keeps its input in a hidden textarea, so iOS never
shows the edit menu over it, and commands could not be pasted into a
shell from the phone.

A small Paste button now sits in the terminal's top right corner while
the primary pointer is coarse (touch) and a writable attach is
connected; it is hidden on a fine pointer, on read-only attaches and
while the bridge is connecting or closed. A tap reads the clipboard
inside the gesture and writes the text through the session's aeWrite
(patch 0011): xterm's own paste, bracketed when the shell asked for it,
Enter never pressed. The terminal keeps focus through the tap and is
refocused after. When the Clipboard API is missing (plain HTTP) or
refuses (iOS declined, permission denied, an empty read), a sheet opens
with a textarea where the native long press Paste works; Send writes its
text the same way, Cancel writes nothing. The text is never logged or
stored.

The icon is Tabler clipboard-text from @tabler/icons 3.46.0, inlined in
the new file (four path strings) rather than loading the lazy chunk of
every icon for one button; it draws through AeTablerSvg (patch 0015).

Logic lives in the new web/src/components/AeTerminalPaste.tsx with its
vitest suite. TerminalView.tsx gains an import and one render line.

